# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# V69 M68D (H05-C): newline pinning for BYTE-SEALED artifacts.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# The M62 control plane seals artifacts by the sha256 of their WORKING-TREE
# bytes. That is deliberate: inspecting the bytes that are actually on disk is
# what catches a malicious edit, which a blob-only check would miss.
#
# But Git's own `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows default — rewrites those
# bytes at checkout. MEASURED on two temporary clones of one commit: 0
# control-plane problems with `autocrlf=false` and 131 with it true, across
# SNAPSHOT_CHAIN, RECORD_STORE, SCHEMA, ARCHIVE_INTEGRITY, CURRENT_POINTER,
# AUTHORITY_SEPARATION, VERIFIER_INTEGRITY and INSTRUMENT_STACK. An independent
# Windows run reported the same shape: 147 problems with it on, 16 with it off.
# None of that is corruption; it is a legitimate checkout reporting as one.
#
# The fix is to stop the conversion, NOT to normalise before comparison and NOT
# to recompute a sealed digest from CRLF bytes. `-text` tells Git to perform no
# newline conversion in either direction, so the working-tree bytes equal the
# blob bytes on every platform and a byte seal stays a byte seal.
#
# `jarvis/scripts/verify_m62_control_plane.py` ENFORCES this: its NEWLINE_POLICY
# check requires `git check-attr text` to report `unset` for every byte-sealed
# artifact, so a new snapshot, record or receipt cannot be added outside the
# pin, and a pattern cannot be deleted from here without the control plane
# failing closed.
#
# Do NOT add `text=auto` or `eol=` to anything listed below.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The whole control-plane state tree: current pointer, snapshots, records,
# schemas, migrations, receipts, rulings, witnesses, the scientific manifest.
state/m62/**           -text

# The governed narrative and its sealed historical archive. PROGRESS.md is both
# byte-digested (as the archive's source) and byte-budgeted, so a CRLF checkout
# moves its size as well as its digest.
PROGRESS.md            -text
jarvis/docs/m62/**     -text

# The checker itself is pinned by digest in every generation it verifies.
jarvis/scripts/verify_m62_control_plane.py  -text
